# .dockerignore for the public CryoStack platform/gateway image
# (containers/cryostack/Dockerfile, ghcr.io/icesee-project/cryostack).
#
# Security-sensitive: this file is what keeps user workspace data, runtime
# credentials/state, logs, institutional deployment config, and unrelated
# development/proposal material out of a PUBLIC container image. Treat any
# addition to the repo root as untrusted-by-default for this build context
# until explicitly allow-listed by being left out of this file.

# ---- version control / editor / CI-adjacent tooling ----------------------
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
.gitmodules

# ---- per-user runtime workspace data (never build-time input) ------------
# Live user workspaces (per-user hashed directories at repo root).
/users/
icesee_jupyter_book/icesee_jupyter_notebooks/users/

# ---- runtime state / secrets-shaped files (created at container runtime,
# always volume-mounted in production -- never baked into the image) -------
/var/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*credentials*
*secret*

# ---- logs -------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
icesee.log
relay.log

# ---- build/dist output not needed as build INPUT (rebuilt fresh in-image,
# or belongs to an unrelated release channel) -------------------------------
/dist/
/build/
icesee_jupyter_book/_build/

# ---- unrelated release channel: the desktop Connector client is packaged
# and published separately (build_connector.sh / publish_connector_artifact.sh
# -> /downloads/connectors/); it is not part of the gateway container. ------
/icesee_hpc_connector/

# ---- institutional / production-only deployment config (GT hostnames, AWS
# account-specific CloudFormation) -- not required to build or run the image
# and not appropriate to redistribute inside a public MIT-licensed image. --
deployment/deploy_web_nginx/
deployment/cloudformation/
deployment/publish-cloudformation.sh

# ---- LIVIST submodule (external/living-ice-sheet-temperature): its
# frontend IS now built in-image (containers/cryostack/Dockerfile's
# livist-builder stage), so unlike the rest of this file this is a
# narrow allow-list, not a blanket exclude -- only frontend/ (build
# source) and LICENSE (attribution) are needed; everything else in the
# submodule (Python/uv backend, docs, tests, scripts, its own docs-site
# build, and any locally checked-out .venv/node_modules/dist -- the
# latter two already caught by the generic **/.venv//**/node_modules/
# rules below) is excluded. Do not remove this block back to a blanket
# exclude -- Docker cannot negate a path back in once its parent
# directory itself has been excluded.
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/.venv/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/.cache/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/docs/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/tests/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/scripts/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/site/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/src/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/img/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/.github/
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/*.toml
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/*.lock
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/.python-version
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/README.md
external/living-ice-sheet-temperature/frontend/dist/

# ---- generic dev-environment clutter that may exist locally in any dir ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/.DS_Store
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- explicitly out of scope for this task (paper/proposal/presentation/
# advertising/Auto-config work; not modified, and not shipped in the image)
/paper_/
/nsf-csi-proposal/
/presentation/
/advertising/
/overnight_/

# ---- the scientific HPC/cloud compute image build context is a separate,
# non-public artifact -- not needed inside the platform/gateway image -----
/tools/cloud/
